{{!
    @template report_imagealt/suggestion_summary

    Outstanding bulk suggestion work, surfaced on the report itself.

    A bordered panel rather than an alert, matching the batch page's own progress panel: this describes standing
    state the user can act on, not a message about something that just happened.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * ready - Suggestions generated and waiting to be reviewed.
    * hasready - Whether anything is waiting to be reviewed.
    * generating - Suggestions still queued or being generated.
    * hasgenerating - Whether anything is still being generated.
    * hasmorebatches - Whether the outstanding work spans more than one request.
    * batches - How many requests the outstanding work spans.
    * batchurl - Link to the most recent request holding outstanding work.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "ready": 4,
        "hasready": true,
        "generating": 2,
        "hasgenerating": true,
        "hasmorebatches": true,
        "batches": 2,
        "batchurl": "/report/imagealt/batch.php?id=9"
    }
}}
<div class="border rounded p-3 mb-3 d-flex flex-column flex-sm-row align-items-start align-items-sm-center gap-3"
    data-region="report-imagealt-suggestion-summary">
    <div class="flex-grow-1">
        {{#hasready}}
            <div class="fw-bold">{{#str}} reportsuggestionsready, report_imagealt, {{ready}} {{/str}}</div>
        {{/hasready}}
        {{#hasgenerating}}
            <div class="{{^hasready}}fw-bold{{/hasready}}">
                {{#str}} reportsuggestionsgenerating, report_imagealt, {{generating}} {{/str}}
            </div>
        {{/hasgenerating}}
        {{#hasmorebatches}}
            <div class="text-muted small">
                {{#str}} reportsuggestionsmorebatches, report_imagealt, {{batches}} {{/str}}
            </div>
        {{/hasmorebatches}}
    </div>
    <a href="{{batchurl}}" class="btn btn-primary text-nowrap">
        {{#str}} reviewsuggestions, report_imagealt {{/str}}
    </a>
</div>
